"""AI attribution: this whole file was generated by Claude (Anthropic) in Claude Code, following
design decisions made by the author. See ATTRIBUTION.md for details.

P1 v0.4 decision report for one split (plan 7.2-7.5): every system at its frozen setting, the decision table applied.

Written 2026-11-16 before the freeze (pre-freeze scoring review, item 2):
the decision table must exist as code, run once on dev as a dry run, and be hashed before the single test run.

Systems and settings: ours (L1); rivals B1-strong, B2-local, B2-fast, B2-strong, B3; listen-step baseline T; attribution
L2, L3, T, T0, T0-single; references B2-ideal, VoxTurn alone, No environment, Copy previous. Score systems are decided
with their frozen dev thresholds (th_s, th_r); rule systems give decisions. The manifest says where each system's
outputs for the split are and which thresholds apply:
  dev:  built from the dev outputs and the dev operating points in results/main_v04/dev_report.json (dry run);
  test, replication: built from the freeze file results/main_v04/freeze.json (written at the freeze) and the final
        run's outputs under data/p1v4/runs/final/<split>/ (not written yet).
Decision table (plan 7.4, in order, the first row that holds; "difference" = five-part mean, ours minus rival):
  1 M-listen: for every rival: point >= 0.05 and 95% CI lower > 0; floor mean at most 0.05 below the rival's; unseen
    difference >= 0 (point); and the listen step (7.3) holds.
  2 M-data: as 1, but 7.3 fails.
  3 not M: every rival point >= 0.05 and CI lower > 0, but the floor or the unseen condition fails for some rival.
  4 replication: every rival point >= 0.05, floor and unseen conditions hold, some CI includes 0.
  5 I: every rival either beaten as in row 1 or tied (CI lower > -0.03), and we have a practical advantage over each
    tied rival (it calls an API and we do not, or our median decision time is at most a tenth of its).
  6 S: otherwise.
Listen step (7.3): on the audio-decisive part, ours minus T and minus every rival: point >= 0.05 and CI lower > 0.
Readings of the plan's text (printed with the report):
  R1 floor mean: plan 4.6 lists D and Dk as one row (5 checks); the operating point checks 6 kinds. The table uses the
     5-check mean (D and Dk pooled by points); the 6-kind mean is reported too.
  R2 row 5 checks neither floors nor unseen (as written), so a smaller win can end higher than a larger one that
     fails them (row 3). The report also shows the row under the stricter reading (row 5 with the floor and unseen
     conditions of row 1).
  R3 "beaten as in row 1" inside row 5: the main-comparison condition only (point >= 0.05 and CI lower > 0).
  R4 unseen subsets exist only in test and replication; on dev the condition is "not evaluable" and taken as met.
  R5 "T ties" (row 2's wording): the 95% CI of ours minus T includes 0.
  R6 practical advantage: API rivals (B2-fast, B2-strong, B3) always; local rivals by the laptop latency medians
     (results/main_v04/latency_dev.json).
  R7 intervals: the plan's three cluster factors decide; a five-factor version adding the background-noise recording
     and the user voice is reported for sensitivity (pre-freeze design review item 1).
usage: python -X utf8 scripts/p1v4_test_report.py dev [out.json]       (dry run on the stored dev outputs)
       python -X utf8 scripts/p1v4_test_report.py dev --final [out.json]  (rehearsal of the final path:
              data/p1v4/runs/final/dev/ at the rehearsal record's settings)
       python -X utf8 scripts/p1v4_test_report.py test|replication     (after the freeze; checks its hashes)
Added 2026-11-20 (freeze amendment third draft 4.2 item 3): ours = the main system (step 2d), the old head
becomes the attribution row "L1"; the final manifest reads every path, mode and threshold from the freeze
record; a rival asked for answers only gets its dev answer loss subtracted (amendment 2.6).
Added 2026-11-21 (freeze amendment section 13.1; pre-test reviews):
  - the win, tie and floor constants come from the freeze record;
  - an API rival's setting and thresholds come from p1v4_api.effective (the frozen ones, or the re-choice after a
    failed drift check, which the report names); on test and replication every API score file must have its
    sidecar with no missing question, else the report stops before any metric;
  - a rival asked for answers only: the dev loss is subtracted from the point (only when positive, as before) and
    the dev loss's SE is added to the interval, SE = sqrt(SE_test^2 + SE_loss^2) (three-factor SE for the plan's
    interval, five-factor SE for the five-factor one); the unseen-part difference gets the five-part loss too; raw
    values kept;
  - "plan_as_frozen": the same decision table with the old head ("L1") as ours (the plan's rule before the
    amendment), reported beside the amended one;
  - "by_noise": ours minus each rival on each background-noise recording and with each one left out (described).
  dev --final --modes probabilities|answers   (dev rehearsal only: the API modes for the run, without modes.json)
  dev --final --live-settings                 (dev rehearsal only: settings computed now by p1v4_freeze.settings()
                                               instead of the rehearsal record)
"""
import json
import os
import sys

import numpy as np

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
import p1v4_data as D  # noqa: E402
import p1v4_score as S  # noqa: E402

R = "data/p1v4/runs"
OURS = "ours"           # the main system (freeze amendment third draft 1.1: step 2d); until 2026-11-20 this was "L1"
RIVALS = ("B1-strong", "B2-local", "B2-fast", "B2-strong", "B3")
API_RIVALS = ("B2-fast", "B2-strong", "B3")
ATTRIBUTION = ("L1", "L2", "L3", "T", "T0", "T0-single")      # "L1" = the old head (L1's own decision)
REFERENCES = ("B2-ideal", "VoxTurn alone", "No environment", "Copy previous")
FIVE = S.FACTORS + ("noise", "voice")
WIN, TIE, FLOOR_GAP = 0.05, -0.03, 0.05


def keyed(d):
    return {(k.split("|")[0], k.split("|")[1], int(k.split("|")[2])): v for k, v in d.items()}


def th_of(e):
    return {"th_s": e["th_s"], "th_r": e["th_r"]}


def api_modes(split):
    """The mode of each API rival for this split, written by the test-day probe (freeze amendment 2.2):
    data/p1v4/runs/final/<split>/api/modes.json {"B2-fast": "probabilities" | "answers", ...}. On dev (rehearsal) the
    file may be absent: probabilities, as the stored dev runs."""
    p = f"{R}/final/{split}/api/modes.json"
    if os.path.exists(p):
        return json.load(open(p))
    if split != "dev":
        raise SystemExit(f"{p} missing: run the test-day probe first (amendment 2.2)")
    return {n: "probabilities" for n in API_RIVALS + ("B2-ideal",)}


def final_manifest(split, st, modes=None):
    """Manifest of the final run's outputs (data/p1v4/runs/final/<split>/) at the frozen settings st (the freeze
    record; the rehearsal record on dev). On dev the API rivals are not re-asked: their stored dev scores stand in, in
    the mode api_modes() gives (amendment 4.5). modes: dev rehearsal only, the API modes to use instead of modes.json.
    Amendment 13 (2026-11-21): settings through p1v4_api.effective; on test and replication each API score file's
    sidecar must show no missing question."""
    import p1v4_api as API
    F = f"{R}/final/{split}"
    m = {OURS: {"kind": "score", "path": f"{F}/readouts/scores_{st['main']['name']}.json", **th_of(st["main"])}}
    for n, sub in (("L1", "l1"), ("L2", "l2"), ("L3", "l3"), ("T", "t"), ("T0", "t0"), ("T0-single", "t0single")):
        m[n] = {"kind": "score", "path": f"{F}/{sub}/scores.json", **th_of(st["local"][n])}
    b = st["local"]["B2-local"]
    m["B2-local"] = {"kind": "score", "path": f"{F}/b2local/scores_{split}_K{b['K']}_{b['reading']}.json", **th_of(b)}
    if modes is not None and split != "dev":
        raise SystemExit("--modes is for the dev rehearsal only")
    modes = modes or api_modes(split)
    ans = json.load(open("results/main_v04/answer_only_dev.json")) if split == "dev" else {}
    for n, e in st["api"].items():
        mode = modes[n]
        s = API.effective(e["dir"], split, mode, st)
        if split != "dev":
            path = f"{F}/api/{e['dir']}/scores_{split}_{s['setting']}{'_answers' if mode == 'answers' else ''}.json"
            meta = API.meta_path(path)
            if not os.path.exists(meta):
                raise SystemExit(f"{meta} missing: {n}'s final run did not finish (amendment 13.1)")
            mm = json.load(open(meta))
            if mm["missing"] or mm["setting"] != s["setting"] or mm["mode"] != mode:
                raise SystemExit(f"{n}: {meta} says {mm['missing']} missing, setting {mm['setting']}, mode "
                                 f"{mm['mode']} (expected 0, {s['setting']}, {mode}); no metric computed")
        elif s["override"]:
            path = next(c["path"] for c in json.load(open(s["override"]))["candidates"]
                        if c.get("setting") == s["setting"] and "path" in c)
        elif mode == "probabilities":
            path = f"{R}/api/{e['dir']}/scores_dev_{s['setting']}.json"
        else:
            path = ans[n]["chosen"]["path"].replace("\\", "/")
        m[n] = {"kind": "score", "path": path, **th_of(s), "mode": mode, "setting": s["setting"],
                "override": s["override"]}
        if mode == "answers" and n in API_RIVALS:          # checked where it is used (decision_table)
            m[n]["loss"] = {"points": s["answer_loss_points"], "se_points": s.get("answer_loss_se_points"),
                            "se_points_5f": s.get("answer_loss_se_points_5f")}
    m["B1-strong"] = {"kind": "decision", "path": f"{F}/b1/decisions.json"}
    for n, k in (("VoxTurn alone", "voxturn"), ("No environment", "noenv"), ("Copy previous", "copy")):
        m[n] = {"kind": "decision", "path": f"{F}/refs/{k}_decisions_{split}.json"}
    return m


def dev_manifest():
    """Dry run on the stored dev outputs. Ours = the main system of the rehearsal record (step 2d); "L1" = the old
    head, now an attribution row."""
    rep = json.load(open("results/main_v04/dev_report.json"))
    op = {n: s.get("operating_point") or {} for n, s in rep["systems"].items()}
    main = json.load(open("results/main_v04/freeze_rehearsal.json"))["settings"]["main"]
    m = {OURS: {"kind": "score", "path": f"{R}/readout/scores_dev_{main['name']}.json", **th_of(main)}}
    for n, sub in (("L1", "l1"), ("L2", "l2"), ("L3", "l3"), ("T", "t"), ("T0", "t0"), ("T0-single", "t0single")):
        m[n] = {"kind": "score", "path": f"{R}/{sub}/scores_dev.json", "th_s": op[n]["th_s"], "th_r": op[n]["th_r"]}
    m["B2-local"] = {"kind": "score", "th_s": op["B2-local"]["th_s"], "th_r": op["B2-local"]["th_r"],
                     "path": f"{R}/b2local/scores_dev_K{op['B2-local']['K']}_{op['B2-local']['reading']}.json"}
    for n, sd in (("B2-fast", "b2fast"), ("B2-strong", "b2strong"), ("B3", "b3"), ("B2-ideal", "b2ideal")):
        m[n] = {"kind": "score", "path": f"{R}/api/{sd}/scores_dev_{op[n]['setting']}.json",
                "th_s": op[n]["th_s"], "th_r": op[n]["th_r"]}
    for n, p in (("B1-strong", f"{R}/b1/decisions_dev.json"), ("VoxTurn alone", f"{R}/refs/voxturn_decisions_dev.json"),
                 ("No environment", f"{R}/refs/noenv_decisions_dev.json"),
                 ("Copy previous", f"{R}/refs/copy_decisions_dev.json")):
        m[n] = {"kind": "decision", "path": p}
    return m


def decisions(entry):
    d = keyed(json.load(open(entry["path"])))
    return S.decide(d, entry["th_s"], entry["th_r"]) if entry["kind"] == "score" else d


def floor_means(T):
    """(5-check mean with D and Dk pooled by points, 6-kind mean)."""
    pts = {}
    for u in T.values():
        if u["floor"]:
            pts.setdefault(u["floor"].split("_")[0], []).extend(ok for _, ok in u["points"])
    six = float(np.mean([np.mean(v) for v in pts.values()])) if pts else float("nan")
    five_groups = {}
    for k, v in pts.items():
        five_groups.setdefault("D" if k in ("D", "Dk") else k, []).extend(v)
    five = float(np.mean([np.mean(v) for v in five_groups.values()])) if five_groups else float("nan")
    return five, six


def noise_name(v):
    """A unit's background-noise recording as its environment name (DLIVING, ...); units without one pooled."""
    v = str(v)
    return "no background noise" if v.startswith("none:") else os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(v)) or v


def decision_table(ours_name, tables, sysm, manifest, rule, lat):
    """Plan 7.4 with `ours_name` as ours: comparisons, the answer-loss adjustment of answer-mode API rivals
    (amendment 2.6 and 13.1: point minus the loss when positive, SE combined with the loss's SE, unseen part
    corrected too; raw values kept), the per-rival conditions, the listen step and the row."""
    win, tie, gap = rule["win"], rule["tie"], rule["floor_gap"]
    ours = tables[ours_name]
    comp = {}
    others = RIVALS + ("T",) + tuple(a for a in ATTRIBUTION if a != "T") + REFERENCES + (OURS,)
    for other in others:
        if other in tables and other not in comp and other != ours_name:
            c = {w: S.interval(ours, tables[other], w) for w in ["primary", "audio"] + [f"part:{p}" for p in S.PARTS]}
            if other in RIVALS + ("T",):
                c["primary_5f"] = S.interval(ours, tables[other], "primary", factors=FIVE)
                c["audio_5f"] = S.interval(ours, tables[other], "audio", factors=FIVE)
            comp[other] = c
    loss_subtracted, loss_d = {}, {}
    for o in API_RIVALS:
        L = manifest.get(o, {}).get("loss")
        if o in comp and manifest[o].get("mode") == "answers" and L:
            if any(not L.get(f) or L[f].get(k) is None for f in ("se_points", "se_points_5f")
                   for k in ("five_part", "must_listen")):
                raise SystemExit(f"{o}: the settings have no answer-loss SE (amendment 13.1); remake the record")
            for w, key, five in (("primary", "five_part", False), ("primary_5f", "five_part", True),
                                 ("audio", "must_listen", False), ("audio_5f", "must_listen", True)):
                d = max(0.0, L["points"][key]) / 100
                sl = (L["se_points_5f"] if five else L["se_points"])[key] / 100
                c = comp[o][w]
                c["point_raw"], c["ci95_raw"], c["se_raw"], c["se_loss"] = c["point"], list(c["ci95"]), c["se"], sl
                c["se"] = float(np.sqrt(c["se"] ** 2 + sl ** 2))
                c["point"] = c["point"] - d
                c["ci95"] = [c["point"] - 1.96 * c["se"], c["point"] + 1.96 * c["se"]]
            loss_subtracted[o] = L
            loss_d[o] = max(0.0, L["points"]["five_part"]) / 100
    lat_ours = lat.get(ours_name, lat["L1"])     # R9: ours = L1's forward plus linear read-outs on the same pass
    unseen_eval = not np.isnan(sysm[ours_name]["unseen"])
    per = {}
    for o in RIVALS:
        c = comp[o]["primary"]
        un_raw = sysm[ours_name]["unseen"] - sysm[o]["unseen"] if unseen_eval else None
        un = None if un_raw is None else un_raw - loss_d.get(o, 0.0)
        adv = o in API_RIVALS or (o in lat and lat_ours <= lat[o] / 10)
        per[o] = {"diff": c["point"], "ci95": c["ci95"], "beaten": c["point"] >= win and c["ci95"][0] > 0,
                  "point_ge_5": c["point"] >= win, "ci_above_0": c["ci95"][0] > 0, "tied": c["ci95"][0] > tie,
                  "floor_ok": sysm[ours_name]["floor_mean_5"] >= sysm[o]["floor_mean_5"] - gap,
                  "floor_ok_6": sysm[ours_name]["floor_mean_6"] >= sysm[o]["floor_mean_6"] - gap,
                  "unseen_diff": un, "unseen_diff_raw": un_raw, "unseen_ok": True if un is None else un >= 0,
                  "practical_advantage": adv, "diff_5f_ci95": comp[o]["primary_5f"]["ci95"]}
    listen = {o: {"diff": comp[o]["audio"]["point"], "ci95": comp[o]["audio"]["ci95"],
                  "pass": comp[o]["audio"]["point"] >= win and comp[o]["audio"]["ci95"][0] > 0,
                  "ci95_5f": comp[o]["audio_5f"]["ci95"]} for o in ("T",) + RIVALS}
    listen_ok = all(v["pass"] for v in listen.values())

    def table_row(strict_row5=False):
        all_beaten = all(p["beaten"] for p in per.values())
        cond_ok = all(p["floor_ok"] and p["unseen_ok"] for p in per.values())
        if all_beaten and cond_ok:
            return "1 M-listen" if listen_ok else "2 M-data"
        if all_beaten:
            return "3 not M"
        if all(p["point_ge_5"] for p in per.values()) and cond_ok:
            return "4 replication"
        row5 = all(p["beaten"] or (p["tied"] and p["practical_advantage"]) for p in per.values())
        if row5 and (not strict_row5 or cond_ok):
            return "5 I"
        return "6 S"

    t_tie = comp["T"]["primary"]["ci95"][0] <= 0 <= comp["T"]["primary"]["ci95"][1]
    return {"comparisons": comp, "per_rival": per, "listen_step": listen, "listen_step_holds": listen_ok,
            "row": table_row(), "row_strict_row5": table_row(True), "T_ties": t_tie, "unseen_evaluable": unseen_eval,
            "answer_loss_subtracted": loss_subtracted}


def by_noise(tables, manifest, ours_name=OURS):
    """Amendment 13.1 (described): ours minus each rival (five-part mean) on each background-noise recording alone and
    with it left out; answer-mode rivals with the five-part loss subtracted (raw kept)."""
    ours = tables[ours_name]
    names = sorted({noise_name(x["noise"]) for x in ours.values() if x["subset"] is None})
    out = {"recordings": names, "rivals": {}}
    for o in RIVALS:
        L = manifest.get(o, {}).get("loss") if manifest.get(o, {}).get("mode") == "answers" else None
        d = max(0.0, L["points"]["five_part"]) / 100 if L else 0.0
        res = {}
        for nm in names:
            only = {u for u, x in ours.items() if noise_name(x["noise"]) == nm}
            for tag, sel in (("only", only), ("left out", set(ours) - only)):
                Ta = {u: ours[u] for u in sel if u in tables[o]}
                Tb = {u: tables[o][u] for u in Ta}
                try:
                    c = S.interval(Ta, Tb, "primary")
                except Exception as ex:                  # e.g. a part missing in a small subset
                    res[f"{nm}: {tag}"] = {"error": str(ex)[:200], "n_units": len(Ta)}
                    continue
                res[f"{nm}: {tag}"] = {"point": c["point"] - d, "point_raw": c["point"], "ci95_raw": c["ci95"],
                                       "n_units": len(Ta)}
        out["rivals"][o] = res
    return out


def run(split, out_path=None, final=False, modes=None, live_settings=False):
    """split dev without final: the dry run on the stored dev outputs. Otherwise the final-run manifest at the frozen
    settings (test and replication: the freeze record, hashes checked first; dev with final=True: the rehearsal record
    and data/p1v4/runs/final/dev/). modes, live_settings: dev rehearsal only (see the module notes)."""
    import p1v4_freeze as FZ
    if split != "dev" and (modes is not None or live_settings):
        raise SystemExit("--modes and --live-settings are for the dev rehearsal only")
    if split == "dev" and not final:
        rows, manifest = D.load_rows("dev"), dev_manifest()
        st = json.load(open(FZ.REHEARSAL))["settings"]
    else:
        st = ((FZ.settings() if live_settings else json.load(open(FZ.REHEARSAL))["settings"]) if split == "dev"
              else FZ.verify_or_stop()["settings"])
        rows, manifest = D.load_rows(split), final_manifest(split, st, modes)
    rule = st["decision_table"]
    groups = S.load_groups(split)
    tables = {n: S.unit_table(rows, decisions(e), groups) for n, e in manifest.items()}
    sysm = {}
    for n, T in tables.items():
        m = S.metrics(T)
        f5, f6 = floor_means(T)
        sysm[n] = {"primary": m["primary"], "parts": m["parts"], "audio": m["audio"], "floors": m["floors"],
                   "floor_mean_5": f5, "floor_mean_6": f6, "unseen": m["unseen"]}
    lat = json.load(open("results/main_v04/latency_dev.json"))["totals_median_s"]
    main = decision_table(OURS, tables, sysm, manifest, rule, lat)
    plan = decision_table("L1", tables, sysm, manifest, rule, lat)
    per, listen, listen_ok, t_tie, unseen_eval = (main["per_rival"], main["listen_step"], main["listen_step_holds"],
                                                  main["T_ties"], main["unseen_evaluable"])
    report = {"split": split, "systems": sysm, **main,
              "plan_as_frozen": {"ours": "L1 (the old head; the plan's rule before the amendment)",
                                 **{k: plan[k] for k in ("per_rival", "listen_step", "listen_step_holds", "row",
                                                         "row_strict_row5", "T_ties")}},
              "by_noise": by_noise(tables, manifest),
              "decision_rule": rule,
              "manifest": {n: {k: v for k, v in e.items()} for n, e in manifest.items()},
              "readings": ["R1 floor mean: 5 checks (D, Dk pooled); 6-kind mean reported",
                           "R2 row 5 as written; stricter reading reported as row_strict_row5",
                           "R3 'beaten as in row 1' = point >= 0.05 and CI lower > 0",
                           "R4 unseen not evaluable on dev, taken as met",
                           "R5 'T ties' = CI of ours - T includes 0",
                           "R6 practical advantage: API rivals always; local rivals by latency_dev medians",
                           "R7 decision uses the plan's 3 factors; 5-factor intervals (noise, voice) for sensitivity",
                           "R8 a rival asked for answers only: its dev answer loss (amendment 2.6) is subtracted from "
                           "ours minus it (five-part and must-listen) when positive, raw values kept",
                           "R9 ours (step 2d) has L1's latency: the read-outs are linear maps on the same forward pass",
                           "R10 amendment 13.1: the loss's dev SE is added to the interval of an answer-mode rival "
                           "(three-factor SE for the plan's interval, five-factor SE for the sensitivity one), and the "
                           "five-part loss is also subtracted from the unseen-part difference",
                           "R11 amendment 13.1: plan_as_frozen = the same table with the old head as ours; by_noise = "
                           "ours minus each rival per background-noise recording and with each left out (described)",
                           "R12 amendment 13.2: an API rival re-chosen after a failed drift check runs at the re-chosen "
                           "setting, thresholds and loss (manifest 'override')"]}
    out_path = out_path or (f"results/main_v04/decision_{split}_dryrun.json" if split == "dev" and not final
                            else f"results/main_v04/decision_{split}_final.json")
    json.dump(report, open(out_path, "w"), indent=1)
    print(f"{split}: row {report['row']} (strict row 5: {report['row_strict_row5']}); listen step "
          f"{'holds' if listen_ok else 'fails'}; T ties: {t_tie}; unseen evaluable: {unseen_eval}; "
          f"plan as frozen (old head as ours): row {plan['row']}")
    for o, p in per.items():
        print(f"  ours - {o:10s} {p['diff']:+.3f} [{p['ci95'][0]:+.3f}, {p['ci95'][1]:+.3f}]  5-factor "
              f"[{p['diff_5f_ci95'][0]:+.3f}, {p['diff_5f_ci95'][1]:+.3f}]  beaten {p['beaten']}  tied {p['tied']}  "
              f"floor ok {p['floor_ok']}  advantage {p['practical_advantage']}")
    for o, v in listen.items():
        print(f"  listen ours - {o:10s} {v['diff']:+.3f} [{v['ci95'][0]:+.3f}, {v['ci95'][1]:+.3f}]  5-factor "
              f"[{v['ci95_5f'][0]:+.3f}, {v['ci95_5f'][1]:+.3f}]  pass {v['pass']}")
    print("floor means (5 checks / 6 kinds):", {n: (round(s["floor_mean_5"], 3), round(s["floor_mean_6"], 3))
                                                 for n, s in sysm.items() if n in (OURS,) + RIVALS})
    print("wrote", out_path)
    return report


if __name__ == "__main__":
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    modes_arg = None
    if "--modes" in argv:                                   # dev rehearsal only: probabilities | answers
        i = argv.index("--modes")
        modes_arg = {n: argv[i + 1] for n in API_RIVALS + ("B2-ideal",)}
        del argv[i:i + 2]
    args = [a for a in argv if a not in ("--final", "--live-settings")]
    run(args[0], args[1] if len(args) > 1 else None, final="--final" in argv or args[0] != "dev", modes=modes_arg,
        live_settings="--live-settings" in argv)
